        "original_id": "1311bb7a-b99c-5e8d-91ee-840882d20dda",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Gettysburg, Battle of Tarawa, Gettysburg Address, cemetery consecration\n- Places: Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, Pacific Theater of World War II, Pennsylvania Route 134\n- Topics: American Civil War, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Gettysburg was fought on July 1–3, 1863, in and around Gettysburg, Pennsylvania.\n- The Battle of Gettysburg was fought by Union and Confederate forces during the American Civil War.\n- In 1863, the road later designated Pennsylvania Route 134 was used for the procession to the cemetery consecration where the Gettysburg Address was delivered.\n- The Battle of Tarawa was fought on 20–23 November 1943 in the Pacific Theater of World War II.",
